[[File:Operation_Castle_-_Romeo_001.jpg|thumb|125px|A [[w:nuclear holocaust|nuclear holocaust]] is sometimes associated with modern visualizations of [[w:Armageddon|Armageddon]]]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|grc|Ἁρμαγεδών|tr=Harmagedōn}}, used in [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_%28World_English%29/Revelation#Chapter_16 Revelation 16:16], referring to [[w:Tel Megiddo|Mount Megiddo]], the place of the last battle at the [[w:Last Judgment|Last Judgment]]; from {{der|en|he|-}} {{he-l|הר מגידו|dwv=‎הַר‎ מְגִדּוֹ|tr=har megiddo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˌɑː(ɹ).məˈɡɛ.dn̩/|/-ˈɡɛ.dən/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌɑɹ.məˈɡɛ.dn̩/|/-ˈɡɛ.dən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛdən}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Ar|ma|ged|don}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Christianity|Islam}} [[w:Tel Megiddo|Mount Megiddo]], the site of a [[prophesied]] final battle between the forces of [[good]] and [[evil]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The battle itself.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Apocalypse}}, {{l|en|Final Judgment}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|Ragnarok}} {{gloss|Norse mythology}}
* {{l|en|day of reckoning}}, {{l|en|doomsday}}, {{l|en|judgement day}}, {{l|en|end times}}, {{l|en|end of the world}}

